 "constraints": [],
 "stem": "Find the equation of the straight line passing through the two points $A({=x1}, {=y1})$ and $B({=x2}, {=y2})$. Write it in the form $y = mx + b$.",
 "solution": [
  "The slope is $m = \\frac{{=y2} - ({=y1})}{{=x2} - ({=x1})} = \\frac{{=y2 - y1}}{{=dx}} = {=m}$.",
  "So the equation has the form $y = {=m}x + b$.",
  "The point $A({=x1}, {=y1})$ lies on the line, so it satisfies the equation: ${=y1} = {=m} \\times ({=x1}) + b$.",
  "$b = {=y1} - ({=m * x1}) = {=b}$.",
  "The equation of the line is $y = {=m}x {=sg} {=abs(b)}$."
 ],
